Aizawa may refer to:

== Places ==
* [[Aizawa Prefecture]], a first-level administrative division of [[Okaiken]] located on the northern reaches of the island of [[Ishijima]]
* [[Aizawa, Aizawa|Aizawa]], the capital city of Aizawa Prefecture, historically known as the Port of Fated Meetings
* Aizawa Basin, the volcanic geographic depression surrounding the city that supports local agriculture and geothermal industry

== People ==
* [[Kaito Aizawa]] (1530–1592), a Sanese daimyō of the [[Sengoku Period]] who established the Aizawa free port and negotiated trade with the [[Kingdom of Zong]]

== Facilities and infrastructure ==
* Aizawa International Airport, a major aviation facility and secondary hub for [[Okaiken Air]] serving the trans-Althenian corridors
* Aizawa Metro, the rapid transit subterranean railway network serving the city of Aizawa, noted as the third-largest in Okaiken
* Aizawa Steel Works, a historical shipbuilding and manufacturing company established by Sakamoto Ryoichi during the [[Saito Restoration]]
* Port of Aizawa, the largest freight harbor in northern Okaiken and a vital logistics point for the [[Sanese Imperial Forces]]

== Other uses ==
* Aizawa pepper, a highly spicy volcanic pepper cultivated in the region and used extensively in [[Sanese cuisine]] preparations such as Red Offal Stew